cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the accompanying research article and this software when reusing the numerical evidence."
type: software
title: "Domain Shift Reshapes Accuracy–Efficiency Trade-offs in Progressive Visual Place Recognition: Reproducibility Materials"
authors:
  - family-names: "Abdul Hafez"
    given-names: "A. H."
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, College of Computer Sciences and Information Technology, King Faisal University, Saudi Arabia"
  - family-names: "Alqaraleh"
    given-names: "Saed"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7146-3905"
    affiliation: "Department of Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, College of Information Technology, Mutah University, Jordan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/saed-alqaraleh/gpv-domain-shift"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  This research-software archive provides frozen development and external evaluation
  evidence, integrity checks, analysis scripts and CPU-only numerical replay for
  PlaceGate (identifier GPV) and six comparator policies. It preserves the
  prespecified NO_GO external verdict, 2,499 paired evaluation queries,
  17,493 measured policy-service observations and the 100,000-draw paired
  cluster-bootstrap protocol. The original image-processing pipeline and
  third-party benchmark images are not redistributed.
keywords:
  - visual-place-recognition
  - progressive-verification
  - domain-shift
  - accuracy-efficiency
  - reproducibility
